#: includes/help-page.php:37
msgid "Does the server need ImageMagick or libheif?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help-page.php:38
msgid "No. By default the photo is converted in the browser of the person uploading, and the server only receives a normal JPG or PNG. If your server can read HEIC (WordPress 6.7+ with Imagick), you can let it do the work instead under Settings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help-page.php:41
msgid "Which iPhone photos are supported?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help-page.php:42
msgid "Photos from all iPhones, including iOS 18 HDR photos. The plugin tries the browser's own HEIC support first (Safari), then heic-to (libheif 1.23), then heic2any as a last resort. The Logs page shows which one converted each photo."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help-page.php:45
msgid "Do I have to keep the Tools page open?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help-page.php:46
msgid "Yes, while existing images are being converted in the browser. Background conversion also runs on other dashboard pages, up to 25 images per page load. With server conversion the work still starts from the page, but your device does not do the heavy lifting."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help-page.php:49
msgid "Will my pages and Elementor layouts break?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help-page.php:50
msgid "No. The attachment keeps its Media Library ID, so featured images, galleries and Elementor widgets point at the new file automatically. Links typed into content (including resized copies such as image-300x200.heic) are updated when \"Update old .heic links\" is on."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help-page.php:53
msgid "Is the camera data (EXIF) kept?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help-page.php:54
msgid "No. Browser conversion removes the camera model, date taken and GPS location from the new image, which also stops visitors from seeing where a photo was taken. Keep the original .heic file if you need that information."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help-page.php:57
msgid "An image failed to convert. What now?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help-page.php:58
msgid "Open Logs to see the reason, then use \"Retry failed\" on the Tools page. If your media is served from another domain (a CDN or offload plugin), that domain must allow cross-origin requests from your admin area. Very large photos may need \"Photos converted at the same time\" set to 1."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help-page.php:61
msgid "Does it work for uploads from the front end (forms)?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help-page.php:62
msgid "Not while uploading: conversion runs in the dashboard and editors. If a form plugin saves HEIC photos to the Media Library, they are listed under Tools and converted from there or in the background."
msgstr ""

